=== Dragons ===
An [[Ender Dragon]] can summon large waves of '''Zealots''' when it is weak and the battle has gone on for a long time. These Zealots are hostile towards players.

== Behavior ==
Naturally spawning '''Zealots''' are neutral mobs like {{MobSprite|Enderman|Endermen}}; they do not attack the player unless they are attacked first, or a player looks at their head when provoked. If the player angers them, they will attack the aggressor and regularly teleport behind them to evade attacks. Zealots spawned from {{MobSprite|Ender Dragon}}s are always hostile. They have {{Stat|hp|13,000}} and deal {{Stat|dmg|1,250}}. 

Zealots, like {{MobSprite|Enderman|Endermen}}, cannot be damaged by [[Arrows]] from most [[Bows]] or harmful [[Potions]]; attempting to shoot one results in the Zealot teleporting away. However, magic projectiles such as those from the {{Item|Frozen Scythe|text=Frozen}} and {{Item|Glacial Scythe}}, {{Item|Jerry-chine Gun}}, and {{Item|Explosive Bow}} can still damage them. The bows obtained from [[Enderman Slayer]], being the {{Item|Juju Shortbow}} and {{Item|Terminator}}, can also damage Zealots.

When an {{MobSprite|Ender Dragon|Ender Dragon}} is defeated, all Zealots in the Nest, including Special Zealots, immediately despawn.

=== Special Zealots ===
{{Main|Special Zealot}}
When a player kills a '''Zealot''', there is a chance for a {{MobSprite|Special Zealot}} to spawn nearby.

=== End Stone Protector ===
{{Main|End Stone Protector}}
The [[End Stone Protector]] spawns in a lobby when 5,000 '''Zealots''' have been killed since the last boss. Every 1,000 kills, a message is displayed in chat and more layers of the Protector emerge.

Contributing up to 100 Zealot kills to the milestone increases the quality of loot from the [[Bosses|Boss]].

